  "notes": "Four rods on the diagonals (16 mm from the centre, at ±500 V in planar symmetry: they run without end along z) make a quadrupole field, φ ∝ xy, with a saddle at the centre. A 1 keV Ar⁺ beam entering along the x axis is bent through 90° and leaves along −y, about 10 mm to one side of the centre: the electrostatic turn used in ion beam lines to select a beam or fold an instrument. Raise the voltage and the turn tightens until the beam clips the inner rod; lower it and the beam leaves at a shallower angle. Change the energy to see the chromatic spread, and add a cone to the group for the lens action across the beam."
